  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 27th March 2003 the proposed roof extension at 273 Hounslow Road would not be lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\tThe development does not fall within Class B Part 1 Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995 because the cubic content of the resulting building and all applicable ancillary structures would exceed the maximum permitted development volume of 70 cubic metres, for development to a semi detached dwelling. \r\nA planning application for construction of the proposed development will therefore be required.\r\n\r\n"
